  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an array AAA of size NNN. Can the array be rearranged such that all the (non-empty) prefixes of the array has an odd sum?\n\nFormally, does there exist a rearrangement array BBB of the array AAA such that B1+B2+…+BiB_1 + B_2 + \\ldots + B_iB1​+B2​+…+Bi​ is odd for every 1≤i≤N1 \\le i \\le N1≤i≤N. Output Yes\\text{Yes}Yes if it is possible and No\\text{No}No otherwise.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN - the size of the array.\nThe second line contains NNN integers - A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output Yes\\text{Yes}Yes if it is possible to rearrange the array AAA to make all prefix sums be odd, and No\\text{No}No otherwise.\n\n\nIt is allowed to print each character in either case, for example, YES\\text{YES}YES, yes\\text{yes}yes and yEs\\text{yEs}yEs will all be accepted.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\le T \\le 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤N≤1001 \\le N \\le 1001≤N≤100",
      "1≤Ai≤1001 \\le A_i \\le 1001≤Ai​≤100"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n1\n1\n2\n2 4\n3\n2 1 2",
        "output": "Yes\nNo\nYes",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1 : The given array AAA is already good because the only prefix sum is 111, which is odd.\nTest Case 2 : The given array AAA has 222 even prefix sums. There exists no good rearrangement of the array.\nTest Case 3 : We can rearrange to [1,2,2][1, 2, 2][1,2,2] which has prefix sums 1,3,51, 3, 51,3,5, all of which are odd."
      }
    ]
  },
